    <hr />

    <h2>2026 LPCVC Overview</h2>
    <p>
      The 2026 IEEE Low-Power Computer Vision Challenge (LPCVC) focused on
      efficient computer-vision models that can be optimized and deployed on
      edge devices, including mobile phones and AI PCs. In collaboration with
      Qualcomm AI Hub, the challenge provided an accessible evaluation process
      for models in formats including PyTorch, TensorFlow, TFLite, and ONNX.
    </p>

    <p>The 2026 competition featured three tracks:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Track 1:</strong> Image-to-Text Retrieval</li>
      <li><strong>Track 2:</strong> Action Recognition in Video</li>
      <li><strong>Track 3:</strong> AI Generated Image Detection</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      The formal submission window ran from March 1, 2026 through April 30,
      2026. Teams submitted models through the LPCVC evaluation infrastructure,
      and the public leaderboard displayed the resulting performance.
    </p>

    <p>
      The challenge encouraged practical, efficient solutions for real-world
      edge-device applications. Winning solutions are published openly to
      support continued development in efficient computer vision.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>2026 LPCVC Winners</h2>
    <p>
      The 2026 IEEE Low-Power Computer Vision Challenge concluded with winners
      announced for all three tracks.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Track 1: Image-to-Text Retrieval</strong><br />
      <span style="margin-left: 1em;">1st: EfficientAI</span><br />
      <span style="margin-left: 1em;">2nd: mangojump</span><br />
      <span style="margin-left: 1em;">3rd: Team Manifold</span>
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Track 2: Action Recognition in Video</strong><br />
      <span style="margin-left: 1em;">1st: EfficientAI</span><br />
      <span style="margin-left: 1em;">2nd: team-alpha</span><br />
      <span style="margin-left: 1em;">3rd: CDA-IITGoa</span>
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Track 3: AI Generated Image Detection</strong><br />
      <span style="margin-left: 1em;">1st: OptimAI</span><br />
      <span style="margin-left: 1em;">2nd: SSUPER_POWER</span><br />
      <span style="margin-left: 1em;">3rd: MaXinLab and TigerSecLab (amirsalar)</span>
    </p>

    <p>
      See the <a href="/2026LPCVC/winners">2026 winners page</a> for the
      teams' solution links and additional details.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Workshop and Sponsor</h2>
    <p>
      LPCVC was associated with the ECV Workshop at CVPR 2026 in Denver,
      Colorado, on June 3, 2026. The 2026 challenge was sponsored by Qualcomm.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a
        href="https://ecv-workshop.github.io/"
        target="_blank"
